Package: liblucid-wayland-dev
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libwayland-dev, libglib2.0-dev
Description: Wayland client code shared by the LucidOS shell -- header and library
 Answers "which windows are open, which one is focused, and can I act on
 them" from whichever protocol the compositor actually implements:
 ext-foreign-toplevel-list-v1, the wlroots predecessor, or a /proc walk where
 neither exists.
 .
 The three are not equivalent and the library says so rather than pretending.
 ext- is a list protocol and deliberately carries no way to focus or close a
 window; the wlroots one does; /proc knows processes and not windows, so it
 reports background services as running applications and misses most Flatpaks.
 A consumer asks for what it needs and is told what it got.
 .
 The Wayland protocol XML is vendored because wlr-protocols is not packaged on
 Debian or Ubuntu at all, and pinning it means the generated marshalling cannot
 change underneath a build.
 .
 A static library while the interface is still moving: window_count() and
 activate() were both added in September 2026.
